/*
contributors: Alexander Griffis
description: |
    Metal already provides a native atan2(y, x), equivalent to GLSL's atan(y, x),
    so redefining it here would make every call ambiguous. Use the native function,
    or mod(atan2(y, x) + PI, TAU) for the 0 to TAU range of the GLSL version.
    More about it at https://github.com/Yaazarai/GLSL-ATAN2-DOC

use: <float> atan2(<float>y, <float> x)
*/

#ifndef FNC_ATAN2
#define FNC_ATAN2
#endif
